{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01887",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.37,
      "end_seconds": 5.15,
      "duration_seconds": 3.78,
      "text": "Morning, doctor. Is this the right room?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.64,
      "end_seconds": 10.78,
      "duration_seconds": 4.14,
      "text": "Yes, have a seat. Tell me what's going on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 11.83,
      "end_seconds": 24.21,
      "duration_seconds": 12.38,
      "text": "Okay, so morning, doctor. I'll stay and fill in anything that's missed. It's itchy raised welts, doctor. She didn't want to come, but I insisted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 25.7,
      "end_seconds": 27.92,
      "duration_seconds": 2.22,
      "text": "Did it come on recently?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 28.96,
      "end_seconds": 32.02,
      "duration_seconds": 3.06,
      "text": "I've had it since last Tuesday."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 33.32,
      "end_seconds": 42.25,
      "duration_seconds": 8.93,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 43.68,
      "end_seconds": 53.11,
      "duration_seconds": 9.43,
      "text": "Well, uh, it feels severe to me. It happens every other day. I notice it more with stress."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 55.06,
      "end_seconds": 57.88,
      "duration_seconds": 2.82,
      "text": "Have you noticed anything else alongside it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 59.59,
      "end_seconds": 76.42,
      "duration_seconds": 16.83,
      "text": "Let me think, um, it usually comes with welts that move around. Oh, and poor sleep from itching. So, um, the welts that move around? That's been for three weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 78.35,
      "end_seconds": 81.75,
      "duration_seconds": 3.4,
      "text": "A few quick ones: throat tightness or fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 82.76,
      "end_seconds": 88.06,
      "duration_seconds": 5.3,
      "text": "Sorry, what was I saying, no, not a single one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 89.53,
      "end_seconds": 93.78,
      "duration_seconds": 4.25,
      "text": "A few quick ones: difficulty breathing or joint pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 99.03,
      "end_seconds": 104.74,
      "duration_seconds": 5.71,
      "text": "Um, I haven't had difficulty breathing or joint pain, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 105.74,
      "end_seconds": 108.55,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "How are your bowels, any trouble?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 111.73,
      "end_seconds": 115.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.76,
      "text": "Actually, bowels are regular, nothing odd."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 123.49,
      "end_seconds": 128.69,
      "duration_seconds": 5.2,
      "text": "Has anything ever caused you a reaction? I mean any allergies."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 130.74,
      "end_seconds": 141.36,
      "duration_seconds": 10.62,
      "text": "Hmm, yes, wheat. I've no idea what the reaction was, only that I'm not supposed to have it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 142.18,
      "end_seconds": 145.59,
      "duration_seconds": 3.41,
      "text": "Does your family have any medical conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 148.77,
      "end_seconds": 156.56,
      "duration_seconds": 7.79,
      "text": "Hmm, my mother had a stroke. Ah, my father has Parkinson's disease."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 158.35,
      "end_seconds": 159.58,
      "duration_seconds": 1.23,
      "text": "Any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 161.12,
      "end_seconds": 164.59,
      "duration_seconds": 3.47,
      "text": "Nothing, I haven't had any operations."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 165.56,
      "end_seconds": 170.35,
      "duration_seconds": 4.79,
      "text": "Let's talk a little about your daily life and habits."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 171.98,
      "end_seconds": 186.37,
      "duration_seconds": 14.39,
      "text": "I quit smoking around ten years ago. I only drink at family occasions. I walk the dog every morning. My husband and I live above the shop."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 187.96,
      "end_seconds": 191.79,
      "duration_seconds": 3.83,
      "text": "Do you take any prescribed or over-the-counter medicines?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 193.88,
      "end_seconds": 208.61,
      "duration_seconds": 14.73,
      "text": "So, I take Thyronorm, 50 micrograms, every morning. Yeah, uh, it's something called lisi... lisinopril, 10 milligrams, maybe, once a day for my pressure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 210.46,
      "end_seconds": 214.94,
      "duration_seconds": 4.48,
      "text": "Have you got the box or the prescription on you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 216.55,
      "end_seconds": 224.28,
      "duration_seconds": 7.73,
      "text": "Mm, no, it's at home. It's cetirizine, 10 milligrams, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 225.11,
      "end_seconds": 235.68,
      "duration_seconds": 10.57,
      "text": "Doctor, I think the last prescription for the cetirizine was 20 milligrams. We changed it at the last visit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 236.41,
      "end_seconds": 242.2,
      "duration_seconds": 5.79,
      "text": "Okay. Have you got the newest prescription or the box with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 243.24,
      "end_seconds": 249.65,
      "duration_seconds": 6.41,
      "text": "I don't think I have it with me. Metoprolol I don't take anymore."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 250.23,
      "end_seconds": 253.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.11,
      "text": "Any health conditions I should have on record?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 254.45,
      "end_seconds": 260.52,
      "duration_seconds": 6.07,
      "text": "An underactive thyroid, for about a year. I have high blood pressure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 263.32,
      "end_seconds": 266.29,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "Right, and anything else to add?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 268.14,
      "end_seconds": 275.45,
      "duration_seconds": 7.31,
      "text": "Right, so an underactive thyroid is already on your record. We'll keep that in mind today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 289.43,
      "end_seconds": 291.91,
      "duration_seconds": 2.48,
      "text": "Let me take your readings now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 298.03,
      "end_seconds": 300.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "Nearly done with the readings..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 315.09,
      "end_seconds": 324.12,
      "duration_seconds": 9.03,
      "text": "Okay: temperature 36.7, pulse 69, respiratory rate 18. And SpO2 98 percent on room air, BP is 108 over 75."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 325.29,
      "end_seconds": 327.0,
      "duration_seconds": 1.71,
      "text": "Is that okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 328.0,
      "end_seconds": 330.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "That's fine, I'll explain it soon."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 332.27,
      "end_seconds": 336.76,
      "duration_seconds": 4.49,
      "text": "I'll examine you in a second, make yourself comfortable."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 338.42,
      "end_seconds": 339.7,
      "duration_seconds": 1.28,
      "text": "Nearly finished here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 357.17,
      "end_seconds": 363.17,
      "duration_seconds": 6.0,
      "text": "There are pink raised wheals on the arms and trunk that blanch with pressure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 366.94,
      "end_seconds": 370.35,
      "duration_seconds": 3.41,
      "text": "Right, that's all I needed to check."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 389.21,
      "end_seconds": 407.09,
      "duration_seconds": 17.88,
      "text": "Putting it all together, it points towards chronic spontaneous urticaria. We shouldn't forget a food reaction. Just to be sure I understood. You've had itchy raised welts, since last Tuesday, severe, and no throat tightness or fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 408.22,
      "end_seconds": 410.15,
      "duration_seconds": 1.93,
      "text": "Yes, that's right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 411.04,
      "end_seconds": 437.02,
      "duration_seconds": 25.98,
      "text": "I want blood tests done, that's for chronic urticaria. You'll be taking fexofenadine, 180 milligrams, once a day, long term. That's for urticaria. Keep a diary of foods and triggers and avoid hot showers. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose. Come back in six weeks. That's all from me. Any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 438.82,
      "end_seconds": 441.87,
      "duration_seconds": 3.05,
      "text": "Hmm, thank you, that's helpful."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 442.86,
      "end_seconds": 445.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.58,
      "text": "Alright, have a good day."
    }
  ]
}